WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.230
- I'm 20 years old and I'm
addicted to drinking gasoline.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.063
- Eating bugs.

00:00:05.063 --> 00:00:06.910
- Rescuing food from dumpsters.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.310
- Eating sand.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.140
- People have some strange addictions

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.720
and they actually made a show about it,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.620
and while you may be tempted to laugh,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.200
hear me out in my points
first before going to judge.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.033
Bewoop.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:19.740
- My name is Nathaniel, I'm 27 years old

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.583
and I'm in a serious
relationship with my car.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.490
- Interesting.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.663
- [Nathaniel] Morning, baby.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.210
- It's a pretty car, I'm not gonna lie,

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.090
I'm digging the color.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.430
- It's like it was love at first sight.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:35.980
His body, and then his interior,

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.990
and everything just
together just seemed to fit

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.559
and I just felt an instant connection.

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:43.680
(suspenseful music)

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.720
- You know, this objectophilia
seems like it runs

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.090
in a similar pattern as animism,
where someone believes that

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:53.140
a inanimate object has a
spirit that is living on

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.580
and that's why they fall in love with it.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.580
- [Narrator] Nathaniel's
relationship with Chase

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.740
goes beyond dates and presents.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.753
- We have our times when we get sexual.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.010
Does that feel good?

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:07.030
- There has been some
research that has showed

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.730
a sexual gratification or objectification

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.350
of inanimate objects does sometimes run

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:15.660
in a similar course also with autism,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:18.360
so I don't know if autism
was in fact diagnosed

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.193
in this case.

00:01:19.193 --> 00:01:20.150
- I'm 19 years old

00:01:21.421 --> 00:01:23.021
and I'm addicted to eating sand.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:24.703
- Sand, okay.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.140
- [Brea] I just love the crutch.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.910
- That's not good for the teeth.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:32.720
There's a condition known as Pica

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.790
where individuals actually
crave foods like sand,

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.930
soil, paint, even metal objects,

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:40.160
and there are treatments for it.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.230
- [Narrator] Brea is so dependent
on that satisfying crunch,

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:47.180
she turns to nail files when
her sand supply runs low.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.730
- It has like sandpaper on it

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:51.210
that gives me the same crunch,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.370
so I put it like in the back of my teeth

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:56.210
and just go like this.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.840
- Essentially, you're
sanding down your teeth.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.030
When you grind them down with
that very abrasive surface

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.220
of the sandpaper, you're
actually doing serious damage

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.053
to it.

00:02:04.053 --> 00:02:05.310
I wouldn't be surprised if
she's going to need dentures

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.390
or implants very early on in her life,

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.010
unless this gets addressed.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:12.823
- I'm 20 years old and I'm
addicted to drinking gasoline.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.900
- Gasoline is toxic,

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.640
and I'm not just saying
drinking it, inhaling it,

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.890
getting it on your skin.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.740
In fact, individuals who work
surrounding gasoline vapor

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.740
have higher rates of certain illnesses.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.940
Animal studies have showed
kidney, liver disease

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.590
from extended exposure to gasoline vapors.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:35.120
- I can't go a day without it.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.290
Like, I crave it.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.210
I need it.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:41.360
I'll wake up, go to the
washroom and drink the gas.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.100
- This is super dangerous
because of a compound called

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.150
hydrocarbons found within gasoline,

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:49.280
which actually act as essential
nervous system depressant.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.900
You can almost feel like
you're drunk off of it,

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.110
but the danger that it
causes to your GI tract,

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.150
your vital organs, outweigh
any potential benefit

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:58.983
of consuming it.

00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:01.600
- [Narrator] Stanley
might be 31 years old,

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.610
but for the past 18 years,

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:06.973
he has gone to remarkable
lengths to remain young at heart.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:08.733
Very young.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.290
- Okay, I understand

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.210
if you're watching at home
and you're quick to judge

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:17.130
this gentleman and say, wow,
this is clearly a disorder.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:17.963
Wait.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.800
The way we decide in
medicine and healthcare

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.510
whether or not something is a disorder

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.380
is based on the patient's own life.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.740
If the patient is not having an issue

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.700
maintaining a job, maintaining
healthy social connections,

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.300
maintaining a relationship,

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:36.420
if all these major developmental
aspects of life are normal,

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.253
this is not a disorder.

00:03:37.253 --> 00:03:39.410
We have to be very careful
with our definitions here.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:42.210
- [Narrator] And he doesn't
just talk the baby talk,

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:46.450
he dedicates eight hours a
day role-playing as a toddler.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.280
- That's an important fact to hear,

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.460
because if you have to
dedicate eight hours of the day

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.730
to do this, can you maintain a job?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.510
